# PDC example for a Postfix MSA/submission instance.
#
# IMPORTANT:
#
# 1. PDC must run before permit_mynetworks and permit_sasl_authenticated.
#    Otherwise those PERMIT results short-circuit the restriction list.
#
# 2. Do NOT also use reject_unknown_recipient_domain here unless duplicate
#    DNS checks are intentional. PDC performs the recipient-domain DNS checks
#    itself and provides clearer replies for NXDOMAIN, Null MX, unusable MX,
#    no MX/A/AAAA, and temporary DNS failures.
#
# 3. For minimal external DNS traffic, let PDC and Postfix use the same local
#    caching resolver (for example Unbound or BIND on localhost). Postfix does
#    not pass the result of reject_unknown_recipient_domain to policy services,
#    so those results cannot be reused directly by PDC.

smtpd_recipient_restrictions =
    reject_non_fqdn_recipient,
    check_policy_service unix:private/pdc,
    permit_mynetworks,
    permit_sasl_authenticated,
    reject_unauth_destination,
    permit
